a call changes the world or answers about it, never both. asking must be
free to repeat.

the test: call it twice. if the second answer differs, it was a command
wearing a query's name — pop, next, getandclear.

commands return nothing worth reading. that is what makes a query safe to
log, cache, retry, reorder — and so what makes `programming/declarative`
possible at all.

names carry it: get/find/is answer, set/add/apply change.
